          "content": {
            "id": "8a58ae9c-493e-3882-b8c9-4f9708c82481",
            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "Companies Are Just Now Tallying Up the Impact of the US Shutdown",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Firms with significant exposure to federal spending, government contracts and regulatory approvals are now tallying up the impact on revenue and profit, with warnings ranging from words of caution to guidance cuts.  Clearfield Inc., a manufacturer of fiber-optic and connectivity products for telecommunications and broadband networks, said industrywide fiber supply constraints and delays in the federal Broadband Equity, Access, and Deployment program, a $42.5 billion initiative to expand broadband access known as BEAD, created uncertainty in the community broadband market.  \u201cThe government shutdown did affect bookings and our forecast for a soft first quarter into next year,\u201d Chief Executive Officer Cheri Beranek said during an earnings call.",
